---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import ClosingCTA from '../components/ClosingCTA.astro';

const lastUpdated = 'May 2026';
---
<Base
  title="FAQ · Joe's Barbershop · Hours, Payment, Walk-ins, Kids"
  description="Frequently asked questions for Joe's Barbershop in Bostonia, El Cajon. Hours, walk-ins, cash-only, kids cuts, parking — answered."
>
  <header class="article-head">
    <div class="wrap">
      <span class="eyebrow kicker-rule">Frequently asked · what people ask</span>
      <h1>Frequently asked questions.</h1>
      <p class="datestamp">UPDATED {lastUpdated.toUpperCase()}</p>
    </div>
  </header>

  <section class="bluf" aria-label="Answer capsule">
    <div class="wrap">
      <p class="bluf-lead">
        <strong>Joe's Barbershop is open Tuesday through Saturday, 10am to 7:30pm, at 723 E Bradley Ave Suite C in Bostonia, El Cajon.</strong> Walk-ins are always welcome — no appointment needed. The shop is cash-only with an ATM on site. Haircuts start at $30, shaves are $30, and beard line-ups are $20. Kids are welcome. Parking is free in the strip-mall lot out front. The 10 questions below cover everything customers ask before walking in for the first time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="faq-master">
    <div class="wrap">

      <h2>Hours &amp; Days</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
          <div>
            <h3>What are Joe's Barbershop's hours?</h3>
            <p>Joe's Barbershop is open Tuesday through Saturday, 10am to 7:30pm. The shop is closed Sunday and Monday. Hours are consistent week to week — no seasonal changes, no holiday-week surprises on regular operating days. If you are not sure before making the drive, call ahead at (619) 891-2775.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Are you open on Sundays or Mondays?</h3>
            <p>No. Joe's Barbershop is closed Sunday and Monday. Tuesday through Saturday, 10am to 7:30pm is the full operating schedule. Plan your visit on any of those five days and the shop will be open.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Are you open on holidays?</h3>
            <p>Holiday hours vary. Joe's Barbershop follows a Tuesday-through-Saturday schedule as its baseline. For specific holiday closures, call the shop at (619) 891-2775 before your visit. The safest approach is to call same-day if you are visiting on or around a major holiday.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Walk-ins &amp; Booking</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Do I need an appointment?</h3>
            <p>No appointment needed. Walk-ins are always welcome Tuesday through Saturday. If you want to guarantee a specific time, you can book online at the Square Site link. The shop handles walk-ins as the norm — you do not need to plan ahead to get a great cut.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
          <div>
            <h3>How long does a haircut take?</h3>
            <p>A standard haircut takes about 30 minutes. A shave or beard service adds 20 to 30 minutes on top. A haircut-plus-beard combo typically runs 45 to 60 minutes total. Walk in with enough time and you will be taken care of without feeling rushed.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">06</span>
          <div>
            <h3>How long is the wait for a walk-in?</h3>
            <p>Wait times depend on how many customers are ahead of you. Busy periods are typically late afternoon on Fridays and Saturdays. Early weekday mornings tend to be faster. If you are concerned about the wait, call (619) 891-2775 to ask how full the shop is before driving over.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Payment &amp; Cash</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">07</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Do you take cards?</h3>
            <p>Cash only. Joe's Barbershop does not accept credit or debit cards for in-shop services. There is an ATM on site if you need it. The ATM fee is charged by the machine, not by the shop. Bringing $30 to $50 in cash covers any service on the menu.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">08</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Do you accept Venmo, Cash App, or Zelle?</h3>
            <p>No digital payment apps are accepted for in-shop services. Cash is the only payment method. The on-site ATM handles cash withdrawals if you arrive without enough. Prices are fixed and visible on the board: haircut $30, shave $30, beard line-up $20, clean-up $15, haircut-plus-beard $50.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">09</span>
          <div>
            <h3>How much does a haircut cost?</h3>
            <p>A standard haircut is $30. A shave is $30. A beard line-up is $20. A clean-up is $15. A haircut-plus-beard combo is $50. All prices are on the board before you sit down. No hidden fees, no upsell pressure. The price you see is what you pay.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Kids &amp; Family</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">10</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Do you cut kids' hair?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Joe's Barbershop is a family-friendly shop. Kids cuts are welcome. The shop serves families who bring dad and the kids in on the same visit. Walk-ins apply the same way — no separate kids appointment needed. Kids cuts are priced the same as adult cuts at $30.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">11</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Is the shop welcoming to kids and families?</h3>
            <p>Yes. Joe's Barbershop is a neighborhood shop that serves East County families. Kids come in with their parents regularly. The atmosphere is relaxed and straightforward — no appointment pressure, no upscale grooming-lounge feel. If you are bringing your kid for their first barbershop cut, this is the kind of shop where that goes fine.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

      <h2>Parking &amp; Location</h2>
      <div class="faq-list">
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">12</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Where is Joe's Barbershop?</h3>
            <p>Joe's Barbershop is at 723 E Bradley Ave, Suite C, El Cajon CA 92021 — in the Bostonia neighborhood, in a strip mall on Bradley Avenue. The shop is accessible from the 8 freeway via the Greenfield Drive or Johnson Avenue exits. Address for navigation: 723 E Bradley Ave, El Cajon CA 92021.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">13</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Where do I park?</h3>
            <p>Free parking is available in the strip-mall lot directly in front of the shop. The lot is shared with other businesses in the same plaza. Parking is typically easy to find. There is no paid parking or parking garage involved — pull in, park, walk in.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
        <article class="faq-q">
          <span class="num" aria-hidden="true">14</span>
          <div>
            <h3>Is Joe's in El Cajon proper or Bostonia?</h3>
            <p>The shop is in Bostonia, which is a community within the El Cajon area of East County San Diego. The mailing address uses El Cajon as the city. Bostonia is on Bradley Avenue, east of downtown El Cajon. Both "Joe's Barbershop El Cajon" and "Joe's Barbershop Bostonia" will get you to the right place: 723 E Bradley Ave, Suite C.</p>
          </div>
        </article>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

  <ClosingCTA />
</Base>

<style>
  .article-head { padding: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px) 0 clamp(32px, 4vw, 48px); background: var(--bg); }
  .article-head .wrap { max-width: 820px; }
  .article-head h1 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(40px, 5vw, 68px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.02; letter-spacing: -0.008em; margin: 0 0 18px; }
  .article-head .datestamp { font-family: var(--font-board); text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.16em; font-size: 11.5px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--muted); margin: 0; }

  .bluf { background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--border); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--border); border-left: 3px solid var(--accent); padding-block: clamp(40px, 5vw, 64px); }
  .bluf .wrap { max-width: 820px; }
  .bluf .bluf-lead { font-size: 18px; line-height: 1.6; max-width: 66ch; margin: 0; }
  .bluf .bluf-lead strong { font-weight: 600; }

  .faq-master { background: var(--bg); padding: clamp(56px, 7vw, 96px) 0; }
  .faq-master .wrap { max-width: 980px; }
  .faq-master h2 {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-size: clamp(28px, 3vw, 36px);
    font-weight: 600;
    margin: 56px 0 24px;
  }
  .faq-master h2:first-of-type { margin-top: 0; }

  /* Replicated from FAQ.astro lines 51-57 — UI-SPEC: do NOT modify FAQ.astro */
  .faq-list { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 32px; max-width: 980px; }
  .faq-q { padding-top: 22px; border-top: 1px solid var(--border); display: grid; grid-template-columns: 60px 1fr; gap: 32px; }
  .faq-q .num { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: 28px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--accent); line-height: 1; }
  .faq-q h3 { font-family: var(--font-display); font-size: clamp(22px, 2.2vw, 28px); font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.2; letter-spacing: -0.005em; margin: 0 0 12px; }
  .faq-q p { margin: 0; font-size: 16.5px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--fg); max-width: 70ch; }
</style>
